DBG-QUALITY raw {"q":"A customer opened a P2 ticket asking for an export of their personal data. What deadline applies to delivering the export?","searches":[{"query":"customer request export of personal data deadline delivery"},{"query":"P2 ticket priority deadline response time"}],"rawFinal":"Export requests deliver data in a machine-readable format (CSV or JSON) within 30 days. [4]\n\nThe standard response window is 30 days from the request date (the date the request is logged with all required information). [4]\n\nNorthwind responds within 30 days; where a request is complex or the volume is large, the response can be extended by up to 60 days, with notice to the requester. [2]\n\nA request is not a ticket: it does not run on the Support SLA Policy clock, it runs on the 30-day response window. [6]\n\nSo the P2 ticket's 3-business-day resolution target does not govern this request; the export must be delivered within 30 days of the request date, extendable by up to 60 days for complex or voluminous requests with notice.","grounded":"A citation in the draft answer did not match evidence retrieved in this turn, so the answer was refused.","ev":[["[1]","nw_legal_data_retention","Customer Data"],["[2]","nw_legal_privacy_policy","Individual Rights"],["[3]","nw_support_dsar_process","What Is a Data Access Request"],["[4]","nw_support_dsar_process","Response Windows"],["[5]","nw_support_dsar_process","Relationship to Other Policies"],["[6]","nw_support_dsar_process","How Requests Arrive"],["[7]","nw_engineering_api_standards","Integration Requirements"],["[8]","nw_finance_refund_policy","Refund and Data"],["[9]","nw_hr_onboarding_guide","Weeks Two Through Four: Role Ramp"],["[10]","nw_support_sla_policy","P2 and P3 Tickets"],["[11]","nw_support_sla_policy","Response and Resolution Targets"],["[12]","nw_support_ticket_priority","Communication Standards"],["[13]","nw_support_channels_hours","Response Expectations by Channel"],["[14]","nw_hr_onboarding_guide","Weeks Two Th